WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.989
I would tell people that in my heart I want
to stop with these military interventions.

00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:34.060
In my heart I don't wanna send our men and
service women to lose their lives.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:39.679
And I don't want them to be responsible for
what ultimately are thousands of innocent

00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:42.320
people being killed in these countries.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.140
So Hillary Clinton dots the Is and crosses
the Ts on all of the pol- all of the names

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:53.000
and everything associated with this, but as
a result of that we have the foreign policy

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.060
that we have right now, that I have to tell
you: I think is horrible, horrible!

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:04.350
And that's how I would answer it tonight.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:09.490
I would be mad, I would be angry, I would
be angry that people would be calling me out

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:17.960
on the names or geographic locations, names
of foreign leaders, when the underlying policy

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.500
has thousands of people dying.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.140
And that is unacceptable.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.700
This is the Gary Johnson that you would have
seen in the debates.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.630
It angers me to no end.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.939
Because what I'm saying, I think, echoes what
most people think.

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:40.750
That what we do is ridiculous.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.510
What we do is abhorrent.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.300
Because that has to do everything- to do everything
with the fact that,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.700
that both of them are vilified.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.840
Both of them are unpopular.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.880
60% of Americans view them negatively.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.210
I think it's pretty clear that we don't have
a qualitative problem with the ticket, we

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.050
have only a quantitative problem, which is
getting known by

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.990
50% of the electorate instead of 30%.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:21.500
And if we go to 50% recognition, we'll go
to 25% ballot preference because Gary doesn't

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.260
have the negatives that the two major party
candidates seem to have.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.880
It's pretty straightforward.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.640
Well, you know, we tell our story.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:43.760
It's a matter of going around and trying to
persuade the national media, among others,

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.740
as well as the people that we see every day
that we offer an alternative to the two establishment

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:54.680
parties and that we're fiscally responsible
and that we're socially inclusive.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.840
Both of which things we've proved to our 2
terms, each of us, in office.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.520
So the difference between us and brand A and
brand B is that we've been there and done

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.580
that and nobody can argue that we didn't change
our states.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:15.080
And we were Republican governors in Democratic
states so, by definition, we had to work across

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.760
the aisle to get our programs enacted.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.760
And we did it, we both moved our states in
more conservative directions fiscally.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.040
Nobody can dispute that.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.440
So, you know, hope is not a plan.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.640
We have a plan and it's to do what we have
already done.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.920
Well I think that we, because of the tools
that we do have available, Twitter being right

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.950
at the top of the list, that we are able to
communicate.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.180
And thank you for that.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.120
So this really is a year of social media.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.300
It's not a year where bought and paid for
advertising in the last weeks of the campaign

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.210
is gonna swing the election because people
will tune that out.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:15.220
You know, once you get past 1215 gross rating
points per week so every man, woman, dog and

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.200
cat has heard the ad, you know, 17 times.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.200
People are gonna say 'no'.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.480
And I think decisions get made virally, social
media and across the fence.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.789
We have- We have understood today that Hillary
is spending 18 million dollars right now

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:31.990
to discredit us.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:40.130
That is more money then we will end up, probably,
having in the campaign to conduct our campaign.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.040
That it's- That it's just, it's horrible.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.040
Why would you even say that?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:03.210
We're giving people a chance to vote for something
as opposed to the lesser of two evils.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.849
That's what we are- that's what we are providing.

00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:07.110
First Vote.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.850
You wanna waste your vote with Hillary or
Clin- or Trump,

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.830
go right ahead and waste your vote.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.170
We're not spoilers we are the first vote.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.610
Last question, please, anybody else?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.499
So I guess we should drop out.

00:05:20.499 --> 00:05:24.610
Is that what you're saying, is that your editorial
here is that we should drop out?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:29.430
Another way of putting it is that this is
a year when the voters really, because of

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.400
a constellation of stars, the voters do have
to think for themselves.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:37.870
And we think if they do think for themselves
that they'll recognize that we're the highway

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:44.330
up the middle, which is fiscally conservative
and socially liberal which is about 60% of

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.949
the people in the United States.

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:48.820
In business terms that's a pretty good addressable
market.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.610
So it's a question of getting that story out
there, we'd love to be on the stage tonight,

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.970
but failing that we're grateful for the chance
to tell our story through this medium.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:17.820
I do.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:22.840
I absolutely believe that if we were just
given top line polling that we would be in

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:23.929
the debates.

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:27.529
Thanks so much guys, really appreciate it.

